<html>
    <head>
        <title>Crispy CRISPR</title>
        <style type="text/css" media="all">@import "/CrispyCrunch/design.css";</style>
        
    </head>
    <body>
        <a name='results'></a>
        <h1>Crispy CRISPR predictions</h1>
        <p>
        Note: If you need help interpreting this result table, see documentation section below prediction table or click <a href='#doc'>here</a>.
        </p>
        <TMPL_IF name='CRISPR_LIST'>
            <form name = 'edit' method='post'>
                <input type='hidden' name='page' value = 'crispr_details'>
                <table border=1>
                    <tr class='header'>
                        <td>Nbr</td>
                        <td>Target sequence</td>
                        <td>Spacer sequence</td>
                        <td>Localisation bin</td>
                        <td>Position</td>
                        <td>Internal DG</td>
                        <td>Hybridisation DG</td>
                        <td>Offtargets</td>
                    </tr>
                    <TMPL_LOOP name = 'CRISPR_LIST'>
                        <tr>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="NBR"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="SPACER"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="TARGET"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="LOCAL_BIN"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="LOCAL_POS"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="INTERNAL_DG"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="HYBRID_DG"></td>
                            <td><TMPL_VAR name="OFFTARGETS"></td>
                        </tr>
                    </TMPL_LOOP>
                </table>
                <br />
            </form>
            <a name='doc'></a>
            <h2>Documentation</h2>
            <p>
                <p>
                    Here is an example image of gRNA-Cas9 aligned to a target sequence:
                </p>
                <img src="/CrispyCrunch/gRNA-Cas9.png" width="600"><br />
                Reference: Mali P, Esvelt KM, Church GM. (2013) Cas9 as a versatile tool for engineering biology. Nature Methods. 10:10:957-63.
                <hr />
                <p>
                    Following is a description of each column presented in the Crispy CRISPR design table above:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li class="leaf"  >
                        <b>Nbr:</b> The prediction number. Please note that the designs are sorted by order of preference based on the following 4 criterias listed below:
                        <ul>
                            <li class="leaf" >
                                
                                <ul>
                                    <li>
                                        1. Least number of off-targets
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        2. Position
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        3. Internal dG
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        4. Hybridization dG
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li class="leaf" >
                        <b>Target sequence:</b> Reverse-complement of the spacer
                    </li>
                    <li class="leaf"  >
                        <b>Spacer sequence:</b> The spacer sequence is shown 5&prime; to 3&prime;. This sequence must be attached in 5&prime; to the gRNA sequence 
                        (5&prime;3&prime;Spacer)<TMPL_VAR name="CRISPR_TAIL">
                    </li>
                    <li class="leaf" >
                        <b>Localisation bin:</b> Subdivision of the submitted DNA region to be targeted 
                    </li>
                    <li class="leaf" >
                        <b>Position:</b> The localization in the submitted DNA region to be targeted
                    </li>
                    <li class="leaf" >
                        <b>Internal DG:</b> The folding of the spacer sequence to favor sequence with the lowest potential of generating intra molecular secondary structures
                    </li>
                    <li class="leaf" >
                        <b>Hybridisation DG:</b> Hybridization energy between the spacer and the targeted sequence to favor spacer sequence with high affinity for its target sequence
                    </li>
                    <li class="leaf" >
                        <b>In silico offtargets:</b> Possible off-targets with 4 mismatches (".") or less relative to 
                        the antisense portion of spacer.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <br/>
                Go <a href='#results'>back</a> to result table.
            </p>
        <TMPL_ELSE>
            No valid CRISPR  could be generated using this sequence.
        </TMPL_IF>
    </body>
</html>
